# API origin the Admin Portal talks to (the centralized Express backend).
# No /api prefix: routes are mounted directly (/admin/login, /admin/me, ...).
#
# DEVELOPMENT (npm run dev)
#   Leave this unset. The portal then uses http://localhost:4000.
#   If you do set it, it must be a valid http(s) URL; a malformed value stops the dev server.
#
# PRODUCTION BUILDS (npm run build) -- REQUIRED
#   Set it to the approved HTTPS API origin, supplied through the build environment
#   (a CI variable or your shell), not a committed file. The build FAILS, before writing
#   dist/, unless the value is:
#     - https:// only
#     - a fully qualified DNS name (it contains a dot)
#     - not localhost, not an IP address, no username/password, no query string or fragment
#     - an origin only: no path (one trailing slash is allowed)
#   After building, run `npm run verify:dist -- --expect <the same URL>` to confirm the
#   bundle embeds it and contains no local API target.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=
